messages:
Sam Patel: Heads-up: Zenith POC seeing intermittent SSE disconnects during streaming responses. Jordan reports partial chunks that break client JSON parser. Repro on their React app using an EventSource polyfill. Can SEs + SRE triage?

Jordan (Zenith Health): Yep. When we call /v1/chat/stream with stream=true we get text/event-stream but sometimes connection closes mid-message. Our client errors 'Unexpected end of JSON input' when parsing chunked payload. Happens ~1/5 requests. Node 18 backend, browser front-end. Sample logs:
```
event: message
id: 123
data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"content":"Hello"}}]}

event: message
id: 124
data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"content":" world"}}]}

// connection closed before final newline
```

Priya Rao: Thanks Jordan. A few quick checks: are you using a proxy (nginx/traefik) or any buffering? Also, are you aggregating chunks and parsing only after full 'data:' event? If the client tries to parse raw concatenated data, partial JSON can happen.

Mateo Chen: Saw a spike in infra logs for that customer's lane around the same time. Backend gateway sent FIN after ~10s idle on some flows. Possibly proxy idle timeout or upstream keepalive. I'll pull keepalive and proxy config.

Sam Patel: @Mateo can you confirm our SSE framing from Redwood side — do we flush after each token? Is it possible middle proxies coalesce events and split JSON objects?

Priya Rao: We flush token frames as individual SSE 'data:' lines. But some intermediaries (esp. corp proxies) may buffer until buffer full or connection close. For client parsing, we recommend streaming parsers that process per SSE event and not assume event maps 1:1 to complete JSON objects.

Jordan (Zenith Health): Important detail: they're not using EventSource in production; they use axios GET with responseType: 'stream' on Node and then forward chunks to browser. Could be our proxy or their forwarder splitting. On their Node side they basically pipe raw to client.

Alex K: Is this reproducible in our hosted env? If it's proxy, maybe we can suggest using connection: keep-alive, Transfer-Encoding: chunked, and ensure no Content-Length headers are set.

Priya Rao: Quick workaround suggestions: 
1) Use native EventSource or fetch + ReadableStream in browser and buffer until newline (SSE events end with double-newline).
2) Server-side: ensure you don't re-chunk JSON. Example Node browser-parsing snippet:
```
const reader = response.body.getReader();
const decoder = new TextDecoder();
let buf = '';
while(true){
  const {done, value} = await reader.read();
  if(done) break;
  buf += decoder.decode(value, {stream:true});
  const parts = buf.split('\n\n');
  buf = parts.pop();
  for(const p of parts){
    // parse SSE event lines here
  }
}
```

Mateo Chen: We confirmed their proxy idle timeout was 15s and upstream keepalive 5s for that dedicated lane. Changing to keepalive=30s and disabling proxy_buffering for testing. Deploying change to dev lane now.

Sam Patel: Jordan, can you run the POC while we flip the settings? If you still see errors, grab a HAR + our raw tcp dump (we can provide instructions).

Jordan (Zenith Health): Running now... 100 requests. Still seeing ~2 failures. Attaching minimal HAR snippet and Node forwarding code: 
```
// simplified forwarder
req.pipe(proxyReq);
proxyReq.on('close', ()=>{ console.log('closed'); });
```

Priya Rao: That forwarding pattern can prematurely close if backpressure isn't handled. Suggest using pipeline/pump or util.promisify(stream.pipeline) to handle end/close properly. Also check you're not calling res.end() on client before upstream finishes.

Mateo Chen: Changes deployed to their dev lane. I also set nginx proxy_buffering off and proxy_read_timeout 60s. Monitoring now.

Sam Patel: :thumbsup: We'll also offer a temporary Dedicated config with no proxy between our runtime and the customer's forwarder if they want a clean test.

Jordan (Zenith Health): After applying the pipeline change + proxy toggles, 0 failures in 200 requests. Looks good from our side. Thanks everyone!

Priya Rao: Follow-ups: 1) SE doc snippet for Node/Browser parsing and example code 2) Add recommended proxy settings to the sales playbook 3) Audit our hosted default proxy settings to reduce this class of issues.

Alex K: Great. Sam, please add these notes to the deal thread and update the SOW: 'Recommend EventSource or ReadableStream; if customer proxies, set proxy_buffering off and proxy_read_timeout >= 60s.'

TriageBot: incident created #INC-2025-042: POC SSE frag/parse. Assigned to Mateo Chen and Priya Rao.
